    "result_text": "All 262 tests pass. \n\nI implemented the `timezone` field on the owner response:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `timezone` string property to the `Owner` schema (after `locality`), documenting the fixed region-to-timezone table. This regenerates `OwnerDto` with a `timezone` field at build time.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added the mapping `@Mapping(target = \"timezone\", expression = \"java(formatTimezone(owner))\")` and a `formatTimezone(Owner)` method that derives the IANA timezone from the already-computed locality via the fixed table: `NSW \u2192 Australia/Sydney`, `VIC \u2192 Australia/Melbourne`, `QLD \u2192 Australia/Brisbane`, returning `null` (field omitted) for any other region such as `UNKNOWN`.\n\nDeriving from `formatLocality(owner)` keeps timezone consistent with the locality the response already reports. The full suite (262 tests, including the new `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsTimezoneForRegion`) is green.",
